goal_understanding.excerpt:
 quote style changes for labels containing `"`: quoteattr may pick single quotes; output remains well-formed and ordinary labels stay byte-identical.

New contract:
1. Syntax: `python3 -m py_compile bench/report.py bench/test_report.py` exits 0. 2. Regression suite: `python3 bench/test_report.py` exits 0 with all 21 tests passing — ordinary and adversarial labels, ElementTree parse of every emitted chart, round-trip text equality, no double escaping, element and attribute invariance. 3. Escaping units: `python3 bench/test_report.py EscapingTest` exits 0 (the five markup characters, quotes in attribute values, Unicode preserved, code points XML 1.0 cannot carry replaced). 4. Chart writer: `python3 bench/test_report.py ChartSvgTest` exits 0 (hostile payloads stay text, no attribute breakout, no added element or attribute, escaped text parsed back unchanged). 5. Hero writer: `python3 bench/test_report.py HeroSvgTest` exits 0 (tile, compare and figure text escaped, the unit tspan intact). 6. Command line and datasets through the writers: `python3 bench/test_report.py GeneratedChartsTest` exits 0 (hostile --label over a results folder, the published 0.8.5 corpus parsed chart by chart, `--help` unchanged). 7. Real corpus: `python3 bench/report.py bench/results/2026-10-12-linux-x64-0.8.5 --images /tmp/vc-plain --builds pi-bolt,bun,node24` exits 0 and writes ten charts. 8. No dataset or image edits: `git diff --stat HEAD` lists no file under bench/results/ or docs/images/."}
